# Story 24: Spawning an Agent (50s)
# Hook: Create autonomous agents that work alongside you -- spawn, prompt, and control them.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-24-spawning-agent.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 9

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- your multi-agent terminal.

[00:04.0 --> 00:10.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode. Use ##agent spawn to create an autonomous agent.

[00:10.0 --> 00:16.0]
Give it a name and a system prompt -- the agent is born.

[00:16.0 --> 00:20.0]
##agent list shows all running agents and their status.

[00:20.0 --> 00:32.0]
Use @agent-name to talk directly to an agent. The agent processes the request autonomously.

[00:32.0 --> 00:38.0]
The agent uses its tools to analyze the codebase.

[00:38.0 --> 00:42.0]
Use @@agent-name deactivate to pause an agent.

[00:42.0 --> 00:46.0]
Use @@agent-name activate to resume it.

[00:46.0 --> 00:50.0]
Spawn, prompt, control -- agents at your fingertips.

